beatsync: credits and licences

Code: this repository (MIT, see LICENSE). The sequencer rings, the field, every effect and the menu tones are made by
code in this repository (src/club.c, src/main.c); the ASCII pass (src/ascii.c) is Detexto's (games/detexto), adapted.

Music: the six songs in songs/ (Test Groove, Late Night, Chicago Jack, Filter Disco House, Tech House Groove, Acid
House Rave) are by the author. Test Groove is synthesised by
tools/make-test-song.mjs. The other five were split into stems with Loukai; each package (its Ogg
Vorbis tracks, song.json with its charts, report.json) is written by tools/make-song.mjs (docs/TOOLS.md). The stem
files they were made from are not in this repository.

Fire and smoke: fx/fire.png, fx/fire_mv.png, fx/smoke.png and fx/smoke_mv.png (the fire backdrop's flipbooks and their
motion sheets) are cartwheel-engine's own explosion flipbooks (samples/fx_explosion/assets), generated by its
tools/fx/bake-flipbooks.mjs from noise carried along a known flow: no source images, CC0 (public domain). Every other
part of the backdrops (backdrops/*.cwscene, src/backdrop.c) is made by code here.

The band: models/band_guitar.glb, band_singer.glb, band_bass.glb and band_drums.glb (the rock stage's players) are
skinned characters generated by more-cartwheel-examples' brawler tools (games/brawler/tools/make-characters.mjs and
its modules, every mesh, texture and outfit made by code), MIT (Copyright (c) 2026 Luis Montes), copied unchanged from
its assets/models. Their play loops, instruments, kit and stage are made by code here (src/band.c).

Font: Fira Mono (fonts/FiraMono-Regular.ttf), digitized data copyright 2012-2015 The Mozilla Foundation and
Telefonica S.A., SIL Open Font License 1.1 (fonts/FiraMono-OFL.txt). The game's characters are drawn in it.

Song tooling (tools/, development only, never linked into the game or shipped in its cart; docs/TOOLS.md lists the
versions): @ffmpeg/core (GPL-2.0-or-later), stem-mp4 (MIT), @wasm-audio-decoders/ogg-vorbis (MIT; libvorbis BSD;
codec-parser LGPL-3.0-or-later).

The launcher art (art/) is made from the game's own frames by tools/make-art.sh; its logo is set in Fira Mono.
